---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What does technical SEO involve for Birmingham companies?',
    a: 'Technical SEO encompasses the infrastructure-level factors that determine whether search engines can efficiently crawl, index, and rank a website. For Birmingham businesses competing across manufacturing, professional services, and retail, weak technical foundations result in lost rankings across both traditional and AI-driven search platforms.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does a technical SEO audit typically take?',
    a: 'Our team completes a thorough technical audit within 5 to 10 working days, depending on site scale and complexity. Large e-commerce platforms with thousands of product pages require more time than a 20-page corporate brochure site.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does technical SEO cost in Birmingham?',
    a: 'Technical SEO audits begin at £500 for small business websites. Ongoing technical SEO retainers for Birmingham organisations typically range from £500 to £2,000 per month, determined by site complexity and the scope of remediation required.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does technical SEO affect AI search visibility?',
    a: 'Yes. AI search platforms such as Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT, and Perplexity depend on well-structured, fast-loading pages with clean markup. Technical SEO ensures a site is machine-readable and eligible for citation in AI-generated responses.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What are Core Web Vitals and how do they impact rankings?',
    a: 'Core Web Vitals are Google\'s quantitative benchmarks for page experience: Largest Contentful Paint measures loading speed, Interaction to Next Paint measures responsiveness, and Cumulative Layout Shift measures visual stability. They are a confirmed ranking factor and directly affect user experience on any Birmingham business website.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is technical SEO necessary for WordPress sites?',
    a: 'WordPress sites frequently require technical SEO intervention. Common issues include bloated plugins degrading page speed, duplicate content generated by tag and category archives, poor mobile rendering, and absent structured data. A technical audit systematically identifies and resolves these problems.',
  },
];

const serviceSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'Technical SEO Birmingham',
  description: 'Technical SEO services for Birmingham businesses including site audits, Core Web Vitals optimisation, crawlability fixes, and structured data implementation.',
  provider: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Colmore SEO',
    url: 'https://seo-birmingham.uk',
    sameAs: [],
    areaServed: {
      '@type': 'City',
      name: 'Birmingham',
      containedInPlace: { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'West Midlands' },
    },
  },
  serviceType: 'Technical SEO',
  areaServed: {
    '@type': 'City',
    name: 'Birmingham',
    containedInPlace: { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'West Midlands' },
  },
  offers: {
    '@type': 'Offer',
    price: '500',
    priceCurrency: 'GBP',
    priceSpecification: {
      '@type': 'UnitPriceSpecification',
      price: '500',
      priceCurrency: 'GBP',
      unitText: 'per audit',
      description: 'Starting from £500 per technical SEO audit',
    },
  },
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
  })),
};
---

<Base
  title="Technical SEO Birmingham | Colmore SEO"
  description="Technical SEO services for Birmingham businesses. Site speed, Core Web Vitals, crawlability, structured data, and mobile-first audits from £500."
  schema={[serviceSchema, faqSchema]}
  ogType="website"
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 prose">
    <h1>Technical SEO Birmingham</h1>

    <p>Technical SEO determines whether search engines can find, crawl, and rank a website. Without robust technical infrastructure, content quality and backlink authority count for nothing. Our team delivers systematic technical SEO for Birmingham businesses operating across Google, Bing, and AI search platforms.</p>

    <div class="quick-answer">
      <strong>Quick Answer:</strong> Technical SEO eliminates the invisible barriers preventing search engines from indexing a site correctly. For Birmingham organisations, this means faster page speeds, clean site architecture, validated structured data, and mobile-first design that converts local searchers into clients. Audits start from <a href="/seo-pricing-birmingham/">£500</a>.
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2>What Technical SEO Delivers for Birmingham Organisations</h2>

      <p>Technical SEO addresses the infrastructure layer of a website: server response times, crawl efficiency, indexation control, structured data integrity, and security protocols. It is the difference between a site that search engines process effortlessly and one that loses ground to competitors with superior foundations.</p>

      <p>Birmingham ranks among the most competitive commercial markets outside London. Whether an organisation operates from the Colmore Business District, trades from the <a href="/areas/">Jewellery Quarter</a>, or serves event clients near the NEC, its website competes against hundreds of local rivals for identical search queries. Technical SEO ensures that competition is not lost on infrastructure failings.</p>

      <p>Common technical deficiencies our team identifies on Birmingham business websites include slow server response times from budget hosting, orphaned pages invisible to crawlers, duplicate content across product variants, and missing or malformed structured data. Each deficiency erodes rankings and revenue.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Core Web Vitals Optimisation</h2>

      <p>Core Web Vitals are Google's quantitative benchmarks for page experience. They directly influence rankings and shape how users perceive a site within the first seconds of loading.</p>

      <h3>Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)</h3>
      <p>LCP measures how quickly the primary content of a page becomes visible. Google requires this within 2.5 seconds. Corporate websites in the Colmore Business District frequently fail LCP due to unoptimised hero images and render-blocking scripts from legacy CMS platforms. Custard Factory startups running modern frameworks perform better but still encounter delays from third-party widget loading.</p>

      <h3>Interaction to Next Paint (INP)</h3>
      <p>INP measures how quickly a site responds to user interactions: clicks, taps, and key presses. E-commerce sites serving Birmingham's Bullring and Grand Central often struggle with INP because of heavy JavaScript from product filtering, live stock checkers, and payment integrations.</p>

      <h3>Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)</h3>
      <p>CLS tracks unexpected visual movement during page load. When elements shift position, users lose confidence. This is particularly damaging for service businesses where layout instability causes visitors to click incorrect elements or abandon the page entirely.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Crawlability and Indexation</h2>

      <p>If search engines cannot crawl a site efficiently, its pages will not appear in results regardless of content quality. Crawlability issues are among the most frequent technical problems our team diagnoses in <a href="/seo-audit-birmingham/">Birmingham SEO audits</a>.</p>

      <h3>Common Crawl Issues in Birmingham E-Commerce</h3>
      <p>Birmingham has a thriving retail and e-commerce sector, from independent Jewellery Quarter retailers selling online to Bullring brands expanding into direct-to-consumer channels. These sites frequently suffer from:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Faceted navigation generating thousands of duplicate URLs that waste crawl budget</li>
        <li>Session IDs appended to URLs, creating infinite crawl loops</li>
        <li>Orphaned product pages from discontinued stock that remain indexed</li>
        <li>Pagination handled without proper rel=next/prev or canonical signals</li>
        <li>Broken internal links from site redesigns or platform migrations</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Indexation Control</h3>
      <p>Not every page on a site warrants indexation. Admin pages, staging environments, thin filter pages, and internal search results dilute quality signals. We implement precise indexation controls using robots.txt directives, meta robots tags, and canonical URLs to ensure Google only indexes pages that deserve to rank.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Structured Data and Schema Markup</h2>

      <p>Structured data communicates to search engines exactly what content represents. For Birmingham businesses, correct schema markup triggers rich results that measurably increase click-through rates.</p>

      <h3>Essential Schema Types for Birmingham Companies</h3>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Schema Type</th>
            <th>Best For</th>
            <th>Rich Result</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>LocalBusiness</td>
            <td>Any Birmingham business with a physical location</td>
            <td>Knowledge panel, local pack</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Product</td>
            <td>Jewellery Quarter retailers, Bullring e-commerce</td>
            <td>Price, availability, reviews in SERPs</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Service</td>
            <td>Professional services, Colmore consultancies</td>
            <td>Service details in knowledge panel</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>FAQPage</td>
            <td>Any page with frequently asked questions</td>
            <td>Expandable FAQ in search results</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Event</td>
            <td>NEC exhibitions, Digbeth venue operators</td>
            <td>Event listings with dates and tickets</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>Our team implements all structured data as JSON-LD inline on each page, following Google's current specifications. Every schema block is validated against the Schema.org standard before deployment.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Site Architecture for Multi-Location Businesses</h2>

      <p>Birmingham businesses operating across multiple locations require site architecture that serves both users and search engines. A solicitor with offices on Colmore Row, in Solihull, and in Sutton Coldfield needs dedicated location pages with unique content, not templated copies with the town name substituted.</p>

      <p>Effective multi-location architecture includes a clear URL hierarchy (e.g., /areas/solihull/, /areas/sutton-coldfield/), internal linking between location pages and <a href="/services/">service pages</a>, and locally relevant content that demonstrates genuine presence in each area. This structure also supports <a href="/ai-search-optimisation-birmingham/">AI search optimisation</a> by providing clear geographic context for machine learning models.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Mobile-First Indexing for Local Search</h2>

      <p>Google uses mobile-first indexing, meaning it primarily crawls and ranks the mobile version of a site. For Birmingham local search, this is critical because the majority of "near me" queries originate from mobile devices used by people physically in Birmingham.</p>

      <p>A user on New Street searching "solicitor near me" expects a site to load instantly, display a phone number prominently, and show a Birmingham address clearly. If a mobile site loads slowly, presents tiny tap targets, or buries contact information behind navigation layers, that potential client goes to a competitor with better mobile UX.</p>

      <p>Our team tests every client site across real devices, not just Chrome DevTools emulation. Real-world performance on mid-range Android devices over 4G connections is the benchmark that matters for local searchers.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>HTTPS and Security Protocols</h2>

      <p>HTTPS is a baseline ranking signal. Every page on a business website must load over a valid SSL/TLS certificate with no mixed content warnings. Beyond rankings, HTTPS protects customer data and builds trust, which is particularly important for e-commerce sites and service businesses handling enquiry forms or payment details.</p>

      <p>Common security deficiencies our team identifies include expired certificates, mixed content from legacy HTTP image URLs, insecure form submissions, and missing security headers such as Content-Security-Policy and X-Frame-Options.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>International SEO for Birmingham Manufacturers</h2>

      <p>Birmingham has a substantial export-oriented manufacturing sector, from precision engineering in Aston to automotive components across the wider West Midlands. Businesses selling internationally require technical SEO that handles multiple languages and regional targeting correctly.</p>

      <p>This includes hreflang implementation to signal language and regional variants to Google, country-specific domain or subdirectory strategies, currency and unit localisation, and server-side content negotiation. Incorrect hreflang configuration can result in the German version of a product page outranking the English version for UK searchers, or the reverse.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Technical SEO and AI Search Visibility</h2>

      <p>AI search platforms such as Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT, and Perplexity crawl and cite well-structured websites. The technical foundations that support traditional search engines also enable AI models to understand and reference content accurately.</p>

      <p>Clean HTML semantics, comprehensive schema markup, fast page speeds, and logical site architecture all contribute to AI search visibility. Sites with poor technical health are less likely to be crawled by AI training pipelines and less likely to be cited in AI-generated responses. Our <a href="/ai-search-optimisation-birmingham/">AI search optimisation</a> page covers this in detail.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="cta-box">
      <h2 style="color: white; margin-top: 0;">Request a Technical SEO Audit</h2>
      <p>Identify exactly what is holding your site back. Our technical audit covers speed, crawlability, structured data, mobile experience, and security.</p>
      <a href="/seo-audit-birmingham/">Request a Proposal</a>
    </div>

    <section class="faq-section">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      {faqs.map((faq) => (
        <details>
          <summary>{faq.q}</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>{faq.a}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Related Services</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/">SEO Birmingham</a> — full SEO services overview</li>
        <li><a href="/services/">All SEO Services</a></li>
        <li><a href="/seo-audit-birmingham/">SEO Audit Birmingham</a> — comprehensive site audit</li>
        <li><a href="/ai-search-optimisation-birmingham/">AI Search Optimisation Birmingham</a></li>
        <li><a href="/industries/">Industry-Specific SEO</a></li>
        <li><a href="/seo-pricing-birmingham/">SEO Pricing</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
